// The `range` namespace (area 19, "Ranges"). Each operation is listed,
// typed, in `jadpo-std`'s operation table, which names the Rust function
// in `jadpo-value` that runs it; a test holds these stubs to that table.
//
// Each follows the range's own end rule: an `InstantRange` holds every
// instant from its start up to, not including, its end. They take an
// `InstantRange` until `Range<T>` comes to the contract (chunk 5.5c2) and
// `DateRange` with the time types (5.5k).

public library range {
    /// Whether `value` is inside `range`.
    function contains(range: InstantRange, value: Instant) -> Bool {}

    /// Whether `a` and `b` share at least one instant.
    function overlaps(a: InstantRange, b: InstantRange) -> Bool {}

    /// The part `a` and `b` share; `none` when they don't overlap.
    function intersection(a: InstantRange, b: InstantRange) -> InstantRange? {}
}
